From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 01:30:30 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 09/12] kcm_virtualkeyboard: mode combo in a page header, KWin
 mode read asynchronously

Page type: Gallery (docs/page-design.md 5). Config keys (kwinrc Wayland/InputMethod), the D-Bus property
org.kde.kwin.VirtualKeyboard.mode and its save path are unchanged.

Moved / renamed:
- The combo "Show Virtual Keyboard:" was a toolbar display component; it is now a FormLayout row in the page header
  above the grid (a labelled control instead of a toolbar item). Label "Show virtual keyboard:" (sentence case),
  entries "With touch and tablet" / "With touch, tablet and mouse" (were Title Case). Row kcm_virtualkeyboard/InputMethod.
- Combo has Accessible.name. Grid, selection and double-click-to-save unchanged. Relabel: inventory/relabel/kcm_virtualkeyboard.tsv.
- OverlayVirtualKeyboardOnWindows stays config-only (no UI existed). Inventory --strict: 0 lost.
HIG ids: HIG-001/005, HIG-019, HIG-058 (labelled control, sentence case).

Speed cause (code): the KcmVirtualKeyboard constructor read the mode with the generated proxy's mode(), a blocking D-Bus
property call to KWin (kcmvirtualkeyboard.cpp:29), so the first frame waited on KWin (or its activation). Now the mode starts
at KWin's default (TouchOnly), an async Properties.Get fills it in, and a user edit made before the answer wins
(m_modeEdited). VirtualKeyboardsModel still runs KApplicationTrader::query synchronously (sycoca, in memory); left as is.
After-numbers: pending, manager will measure. Not built yet. Unconfirmed without a build: that header: accepts a
ColumnLayout with a FormLayout in GridViewKCM (documented as "header: Item").

